I've discovered that it greatly simplifies things
to say that each arm of an IF must be some kind of goto
and that's all.  There were only about 3 IFs in the file
which were not like this already, and I changed them around.

This gets rid of lots of problems.
One problem is what to do about same-cycling an IF.
Now, it's clear: the conditional itself happens
on the same cycle as the other stuff.  This is useful
because 1) it is now easy to save instructions by
doing the conditional jump at the same time as something else,
and 2) the implementation of micropreds is now easy,
because they just same-cycle the body with the IF itself.
There were also lots of uses for same-cycling IFs
aside from just efficiency; for example, in the
conditional-rack-push, which must do
(same-cycle (assert (path load rackpc))
            (if ,condition (goto (literal ...))))

Another problem eliminated is the implementation of
a hairy IF itself.  IF as restricted now should be
very easy to implement.
 
